In vitro fertilization (IVF) devices are specialized medical equipment and consumables used in assisted reproductive technology (ART). These devices create a controlled micro environment that mimics the human body, allowing the combination of eggs and sperm, subsequent embryo culture, and eventual transfer. Core product categories include incubators, microscopes, cryopreservation units, and micromanipulation systems.
