What are IVF Devices?
IVF devices encompass a range of high precision instruments that support every stage of the IVF workflow. Incubators maintain strict temperature, gas (O₂/CO₂) and humidity parameters; microscopes provide sub micron visualisation for oocyte retrieval and embryo assessment; cryopreservation equipment enables vitrification and thawing of gametes and embryos; and micromanipulation tools such as intracytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI) needles facilitate fertilisation at the cellular level. Together, these devices underpin success rates and safety outcomes across fertility clinics worldwide.
