Key Market Drivers
1. Rising Infertility Rates Globally
Approximately 15% of couples worldwide face fertility challenges, a figure driven by delayed parenthood, lifestyle related health issues, and environmental pressures. The expanding patient pool fuels steady demand for advanced IVF devices across both public and private fertility centres.
2. Technological Advancements in IVF Devices
Innovation in time lapse imaging, AI enabled embryo selection, and next generation cryopreservation is reshaping clinical practice. These technologies improve implantation potential, reduce manual scoring errors, and shorten culture cycles, thereby encouraging clinics to upgrade their equipment portfolios.
